@startuml Sequence_5
hide footbox
title Scenario 5: Enemy Turn — Goblin Is Stunned, Skips Turn

participant "BattleEngine" as Engine
participant "Goblin" as Goblin
participant "StunEffect" as Stun
participant "GameState" as State
participant "GameApp" as App

note over Engine, App
  Continuation of the same executePlayerTurn() call as Scenario 4.
  Warrior (SPD 30) already used Shield Bash — StunEffect now on Goblin (turns=2).
  Now processing: Goblin (SPD 25) in the enemy phase.
end note

Engine -> Goblin : beginTurn()
note over Goblin : Iterates activeEffects\ncalls StunEffect.onTurnStart(goblin)
Goblin -> Stun : onTurnStart(goblin)
note over Stun : remainingTurns > 0\nremainingTurns-- (2→1)\nreturn true (skip turn)
Stun --> Goblin : true (skip turn)
note over Goblin : canAct = false\nStunEffect.isExpired()? turns=1 → no, keep it\nreturns false
Goblin --> Engine : false (cannot act)

note over Engine : beginTurn() returned false\nEnemy AI strategy NOT executed\nenemyActed = false — no TurnFrame added

Engine -> Engine : sweepDeadEnemies()
note over Engine : Goblin alive — nothing removed

Engine -> State : checkEndCondition() → 0
Engine -> Engine : endRound()
note over Engine : endRound() decrements specialSkillCooldown (3→2)\nrebuilds turn order for next round

Engine --> App : 0 (continue)
App -> Engine : drainTurnFrames()
App -> App : render TurnFrames from this round\n(only Warrior's Shield Bash frame)

@enduml
